In comparison, the big Rate stack goes in essentially the complete opposite direction. The FC has all the components and connectors on the top side, all the components are covered by a black plastic cover. The bottom side is bare of any components, with a ton of pads laid out in two rows in the front and back, visually completely distinct from anything SpeedyBee has made before or since. The FC also seems to use a novel OSD solution instead of the very common MAX7456 IC (and its many clones).

