### AIO

SpeedyBee [F405 AIO V2](https://www.speedybee.com/speedybee-f405-aio-v2-35-40a-bluejay-25-5x25-5-3-6s-flight-controller/) vs RateFPV [F4V4 40A AIO](https://ratefpv.com/products/ratefpv-rate-f4-v4-40a-32bit-bluetooth-aio)

You guessed it, similar specs once again. Unfortunately, there weren't as many images of the Rate AIO available, I tried cropping some of their product showcase images, but they may be pretty visually busy.

<div class="article-image-grid grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
	<figure>
		<a href="/uploads/articles/rate-isnt-speedybee/aio/rate-aio.webp"><img src="/uploads/articles/rate-isnt-speedybee/aio/rate-aio.webp" alt="RateFPV F4V4 40A AIO with its top cover" loading="lazy" /></a>
		<figcaption>RateFPV F4V4 40A AIO</figcaption>
	</figure>
	<figure>
		<a href="/uploads/articles/rate-isnt-speedybee/aio/sb-aio-top.jpg"><img src="/uploads/articles/rate-isnt-speedybee/aio/sb-aio-top.jpg" alt="SpeedyBee F405 AIO V2 with its top cover" loading="lazy" /></a>
		<figcaption>SpeedyBee F405 AIO V2</figcaption>
	</figure>
</div>

The quickest difference here before even looking at the boards themselves is the ESC firmware, once again a 32bit/8bit split between Rate and SpeedyBee.

Looking closer, the construction here is fundementally different. Speedybee has practically the entire FC section of the AIO on its own PCB that's then soldered to the IO+ESC board. Rate has everything on one board, with the exception of the OSD and BLE modules mentioned before. The fancy black connectors make their appearance again on Rate's board, and on the topic of connectors, SpeedyBee has an antenna connector for the BLE communication, while Rate has an integrated one on their small module, and Rate also offers a receiver connector.

<div class="article-image-grid grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
	<figure>
		<a href="/uploads/articles/rate-isnt-speedybee/aio/rate-aio-top-bare.webp"><img src="/uploads/articles/rate-isnt-speedybee/aio/rate-aio-top-bare.webp" alt="RateFPV AIO top with its main components exposed" loading="lazy" /></a>
		<figcaption>RateFPV AIO, top without cover</figcaption>
	</figure>
